EXT. WINDY HILL - SUNSET

Pip, a very small robot, drags a patched newspaper kite up the hill.

PIP
Today's the day. Wind speed: perfect.

Pip runs. The kite flips, nose-dives, and flops onto the grass.

MOSS (O.S.)
Hoo. You're holding it upside down.

MOSS
Wind doesn't care about perfect.
Let it go a little.

Pip loosens the string. The kite catches the wind and climbs.

PIP
Whoa. Whoa! WHOA!

EXT. WINDY HILL - NIGHT

Pip and Moss sit together. High above, the kite dances among the stars.

PIP
It's flying!

MOSS
No, little one. It's *dancing*.
